  <main class="roam-tour-main">
    <div class="roam-tour-wrapper">
      <div class="roam-tour-badge">8–12 DAY PRIVATE HERITAGE EXPEDITION // 100% SHABBAT-FRIENDLY</div>
      <h1 class="roam-tour-title">Moroccan Jewish Heritage &amp; Mellahs Tour</h1>
      
      <div class="roam-tour-meta-bar">
        <span class="roam-tour-meta-item">📍 ROUTE: CASABLANCA · FES · MARRAKECH · ESSAOUIRA</span>
        <span class="roam-tour-meta-item">⏱ DURATION: 8, 10 OR 12 DAYS</span>
        <span class="roam-tour-meta-item">🕊 100% SHABBAT-OBSERVANT LOGISTICS</span>
        <span class="roam-tour-meta-item">🛡 DEDICATED LICENSED CHAUFFEUR &amp; 4X4</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick Summary / BLUF -->
      <aside class="ai-quick-summary-card" aria-label="Tour Fast Facts and Summary">
        <div class="ai-summary-header">
          <span class="ai-summary-kicker">⚡ EXPEDITION AT A GLANCE (EXECUTIVE SUMMARY)</span>
          <span class="ai-summary-badge">Guaranteed Private Departure</span>
        </div>
        <p class="ai-summary-text">
          The <strong>Moroccan Jewish Heritage &amp; Mellahs Tour</strong> traces over two millennia of Sephardic and Berber Jewish culture in North Africa. Traveling in a dedicated private vehicle with a licensed English-speaking Moroccan chauffeur, you explore the only Museum of Moroccan Judaism in the Arab world, the 15th-century Mellah of Fes, historic synagogues (Ibn Danan, Slat Al Azama, Rabbi Chaim Pinto), the craft enclave of Sefrou, and sacred pilgrimage shrines. Available in <strong>8, 10, or 12-day circuits</strong> with transparent flat vehicle pricing from <strong>€1,450 per vehicle</strong> (covering up to 4–6 passengers combined with all fuel, tolls, and chauffeur expenses included). 100% Shabbat-compliant scheduling with zero travel between Friday afternoon and Saturday Havdalah.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 40px; border-radius: 16px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.12);">
        <img src="/images/morocco-fes-medina-architecture.jpg" alt="Historic Moroccan Synagogue and Mellah Architecture in Fes" style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 520px; object-fit: cover; display: block;">
      </div>

      <div class="roam-article-body">
        <p style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 28px;">
          For more than two thousand years—from before the destruction of the Second Temple through the 1492 expulsion from Spain—Morocco was home to the largest Jewish community in the Islamic world. At its peak, over 300,000 Moroccan Jews lived in urban <em>Mellahs</em>, Atlas mountain villages, and desert trading outposts.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today, Morocco remains the only Arab country with a constitution explicitly celebrating its Hebraic tributary, protected Jewish cemeteries, active synagogues, and state-subsidized restorations of historic Mellahs. Our private heritage tours are curated for diaspora families, roots researchers, and travelers who want deep historic immersion without rigid group bus schedules.
        </p>

        <!-- Highlights Box -->
        <div class="roam-highlights-box">
          <h3 class="roam-highlights-title">Core Pillars of Our Jewish Heritage Circuits</h3>
          <ul class="roam-highlight-list">
            <li>
              <span class="roam-highlight-bullet">✦</span>
              <div><strong>Hereditary Keyholder Access:</strong> Many locked synagogues and historic cemeteries rely on multi-generational Muslim and Jewish caretakers. Your chauffeur liaises ahead with local guardians in Fes, Sefrou, and Essaouira so gates are open upon arrival.</div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="roam-highlight-bullet">✦</span>
              <div><strong>Strict Shabbat Compliance:</strong> On Friday afternoon, we ensure you arrive at your riad or hotel well before sundown. The vehicle is parked throughout Shabbat, and accommodations are situated within comfortable walking distance of active synagogues.</div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="roam-highlight-bullet">✦</span>
              <div><strong>Kosher Provisions &amp; Dining Guidance:</strong> Our vehicles feature a chilled cooler box for fresh foods. In Casablanca and Marrakech, your driver assists with pickups from certified kosher kitchens (Chabad Casablanca, Cercle de l'Union, Kosher Club Marrakech).</div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="roam-highlight-bullet">✦</span>
              <div><strong>Roots &amp; Ancestral Research:</strong> Have family roots in Meknes, Debdou, Demnate, or Ouezzane? We adjust itineraries to locate ancestral family residences, communal archives, and ancestral cemetery plots.</div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>Transparent Flat Vehicle Pricing (Clients Book Own Hotels)</h2>
        <p>
          Unlike group tour operators who mark up hotel rooms by 40%, we operate on a transparent <strong>flat vehicle rate</strong>. You choose and book your preferred riads or luxury hotels directly, while our all-inclusive vehicle fee covers your entire transportation infrastructure: dedicated licensed chauffeur, 2024 luxury vehicle, all fuel, highway tolls, chauffeur lodging &amp; meals, and airport transfers.
        </p>

        <div class="roam-pricing-grid">
          <!-- 8-Day Tier -->
          <div class="roam-price-tier-card">
            <div>
              <div class="tier-badge">8 DAYS // IMPERIAL MELLAHS</div>
              <h3 class="tier-title">Essential Heritage</h3>
              <div class="tier-rate">€1,450</div>
              <div class="tier-unit">Flat rate for entire vehicle (Prado 4x4) · or €1,680 (Mercedes V-Class)</div>
              <ul class="tier-features">
                <li>✓ Casablanca (Museum &amp; Beth-El)</li>
                <li>✓ Rabat &amp; Tomb of Rabbi Raphael Encaoua</li>
                <li>✓ Volubilis Hebrew ruins &amp; Meknes Mellah</li>
                <li>✓ Fes el-Bali (Ibn Danan &amp; Jewish Cemetery)</li>
                <li>✓ Marrakech Mellah &amp; Slat Al Azama</li>
                <li>✓ 100% Shabbat logistics included</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <a href="https://wa.me/212653506441?text=Salam%20Roam%20Morocco!%20I'm%20interested%20in%20the%208-Day%20Jewish%20Heritage%20Tour%20(%E2%82%AC1,450)." class="roam-btn-black" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Inquire 8-Day Tour</a>
          </div>

          <!-- 10-Day Tier -->
          <div class="roam-price-tier-card featured">
            <div>
              <div class="tier-badge">10 DAYS // MOST POPULAR</div>
              <h3 class="tier-title">Grand Heritage &amp; Shrines</h3>
              <div class="tier-rate">€1,850</div>
              <div class="tier-unit">Flat rate for entire vehicle (Prado 4x4) · or €2,150 (Mercedes V-Class)</div>
              <ul class="tier-features">
                <li>✓ All 8-Day destinations included</li>
                <li>✓ Sefrou ("Little Jerusalem") &amp; artisan quarter</li>
